# APKs built for each release: "<suffix or -> <patch set> [<patch set> ...]".
# A patch set is a folder (all its .patch files, in order) or "patches:<first>-<last>" (patches/ by number).
# Every APK starts again from the Eden source in UPSTREAM; all share one versionCode.
#
# Release 31+: Eden PR #4324 (the build Yael plays) + only the speed-ups, no Doris graphics changes: the
# Apex Doris 11 driver fixes the graphics in that build on its own. Own app ID (0001), eden-lun speed-ups
# 0006 and 0008-0026 without 0007 (made water vanish), their adaptation 0027, the device-memory
# continuity fix 0032, and variants/speed: versionCode, Vulkan worker woken only when asleep, frame
# generation resuming 100 ms after a hitch, one GPU wait per texture-cleanup pass.
#
# Main build (release 38+): stock Eden PR #4324 (the build Yael plays) + every speed-up that gives the same results
# as Eden's code, + a safety net for GPU timing. For the Apex Doris 11 driver (14 = same with a log).
#   patches 0006 0008-0027 0032   eden-lun speed-ups (each reviewed: same results as Eden's code; 0007, which
#                                 made water vanish, left out) and the device-memory continuity fix
#   variants/speed                 versionCode, Vulkan worker woken only when asleep, frame generation resuming
#                                 100 ms after a hitch, one GPU wait per texture-cleanup pass
#   variants/report                performance report and hitch sampler (always on; CPU profiler off below)
#   variants/perf36                Eden's CPU topology from all cores, emulator threads on the middle cores (not the
#                                 prime core: no extra heat), shader builders not background, worker hand-off every
#                                 16 draws, staging buffers kept 300 frames, CPU profiler off
#   variants/barriers              real GPU barriers after compute and at wait-for-idle points after memory-writing
#                                 draws (Eden's waits otherwise unchanged): faster emulation changes GPU timing
#
# Release 40 (test): build 38 showed graphical problems again and the eden-lun group is the common part of 32 and 38.
# Yael's current build (35: stock + the three later speed-ups + report) plus one third of the group each, nothing else:
#   -a  memory translation caches, descriptor and macro fast paths, continuity fix (0006 0010 0020 0022-0024 0032)
#   -b  command processing: method sink bypass, dirty-flag skips, register-write batching (0011 0021 0026 + 0027 part)
#   -c  Vulkan and cache fast paths (0008 0009 0012-0019 0025 + 0027 parts)
-a   patches:1-1 variants/speed variants/report variants/lun-a
-b   patches:1-1 variants/speed variants/report variants/lun-b
-c   patches:1-1 variants/speed variants/report variants/lun-c
